<h2 style="font-size: 28px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Overview - NISM Series III-C: Securities Intermediaries Compliance (Fund) Certification Mock Test</h2>
<br />

<p style="color: #000;">
The examination is designed to establish a common minimum knowledge benchmark for professionals engaged in compliance functions across SEBI-registered intermediaries, including Mutual Funds, Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs), Real Estate Investment Trusts (REITs), and Infrastructure Investment Trusts (InvITs).<br>
<br>This certification aims to improve the quality and effectiveness of compliance services by ensuring that compliance officers possess a strong understanding of SEBI regulations, securities market laws, and regulatory frameworks governing the Indian capital market.
It also ensures that professionals responsible for compliance are well-versed with evolving regulatory requirements, enabling better governance, risk control, and regulatory adherence within securities market intermediaries.</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 28px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Your Gateway to a Career in Fund Compliance</h2>
<br />

<p style="color: #000;">
In the intricate and highly regulated world of Indian capital markets, the role of a Compliance Officer is not just important—it is indispensable. As the financial sector grows, so does the complexity of the rules that govern it. For professionals working with Mutual Funds, Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs), Real Estate Investment Trusts (REITs), and Infrastructure Investment Trusts (InvITs), understanding these regulations is the bedrock of their career.<br>
<br>The NISM 3C: Securities Intermediaries Compliance (Fund) Certification Examination is the mandatory, regulator-approved standard for these professionals. It is not merely an exam; it is a validation of your ability to navigate the legal and ethical framework of the securities market.<br>
<br>At clearallexams.in, we recognize the critical nature of this certification. We have designed a comprehensive preparation ecosystem that goes beyond simple question banks. Our goal is to equip you with the knowledge, the practice, and the confidence to clear this rigorous exam on your first attempt and excel in your role as a guardian of market integrity.
</p>



<h2 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Objectives</h2>
<br />
<p style="color: #000;">On successful completion of Securities Intermediaries Compliance (Fund) Certification Mock Test, the candidate should:</p>
<div>

  </p>
  <p style="color: #000;">
The examination is structured into two distinct sections to provide comprehensive coverage of compliance requirements in the Indian securities market.</p>

<p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
   <b> Part A</b> focuses on the financial and regulatory framework of India, offering candidates a strong foundation in the structure of the financial system, key market participants, and the regulatory environment within which intermediaries operate.
  </p>
  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    <b>Part B</b> specifically addresses the rules, regulations, and compliance requirements applicable to Mutual Funds, Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs), Real Estate Investment Trusts (REITs), and Infrastructure Investment Trusts (InvITs).
  </p>
</div>





<h2 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Assessment Structure</h2>
<br />
<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 30px;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="background-color: #e3f2fd;">
      <th style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; padding: 8px;">Component</th>
      <th style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; padding: 8px;">Details</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody style="color: #000;">
